hi I'm Nick Gillespie I'm with Matt  Welch we work at reason and were the  co-authors of the new book the  Declaration of Independence and on ask a  libertarian day the next question is  from Kyle Johnson who asked why has the  libertarian movement succumb to  infighting and self-destruction so many  times in the past Matt Welch three  reasons one some of it reflects a  genuine conflict within self-described  libertarian camp between people who are  seeking a kind of pure philosophical  expression of every question and those  who are trying to figure out you know  how much can we get away with basically  it's pragmatism versus versus the  philosophical bent and that is a natural  conflict that's been there second reason  people who are attracted to marginal  movements or philosophies tend to be  marginal I'm marginal Nick God knows is  marginal and those aren't necessarily  the best people to play well and nicely  with others but third I challenge the  premise of your question Kyle Johnson  I'm not sure that the libertarian  movement has succumbed to anything  whatever it is now I think is  demonstrably greater than it has been in  a long time and partly because a lot of  the people who are libertarian in fact  if not in label they see it less as a  you know exact set of positions that  you're supposed to hold and take it more  of a kind of pre political impulse as  Nick has always said more of an  adjective than a noun and for that  reason that because politics right now  as currently practice is so anti  libertarian on every front there is a  groundswell of actual libertarians in  this country that's much bigger than it  husband yeah I would say that in the  past the infighting and self-destruction  was so huge  because the stakes were so low and that  now the stakes are higher libertarianism  is the surging plurality of Americans  through a lot of different ways people  like free minds and free markets as we  call it at reason  and I think you're going to see not  people going along to get along but the  libertarian impulse will not be denied
 

